      howToRun: 'Start with the question rather than the text and let the room commit to an answer about size. Read verse 16 and let them feel the correction. Establish the jubilee as shared public knowledge before verses 17 and 18, because the whole method depends on the end date being beyond argument. Read 17 and 18 together, gloss reckon and abated as you go, then take the three honesty features separately and ask after each what kind of cheating it removes. Give real silence after the dirt-versus-harvests line. Finish by going round the room for one example each of something they own that is really a term rather than a thing, and send them to the three-line exercise on a real number — including the roof.',
