      howToRun: 'Put the fraction on the board as a real sum before opening the text. Read the three redemption verses in a row without commentary so the uniformity registers, then ask the removal question and wait for the room to get past cost to conversation. Do the round-trip arithmetic out loud with real numbers. State the no-stated-reason limit yourself, clearly, before the room falls in love with the insight — that ordering is deliberate and it teaches the discipline as much as the content. Read verses 20 and 21 slowly and let the sanctuary destination sit. Finish on the two-part rule and send them to write both halves: a number beside every charge of yours that moves, and an end date on every open-ended right, told to the person relying on it.',
